lay B4.\n", "output": "Evaluation: The current hand has multiple terminals and scattered suited tiles with limited potential for chows or pungs. Discarding B4, a single tile with no immediate meld potential, is optimal to maintain flexibility and focus on higher-value tiles like W3 (pair) and F1 (prevailing wind).\nReason: B4 is a lone tile with no adjacent chow partners (B3/B5/B6 are scarce or unavailable). Discarding it preserves the pair of W3 (key for potential pung/kong) and F1 (prevailing wind scoring). This move prioritizes future flexibility and scoring opportunities over low-value tiles.\nAnswer: Play B4"}
